@startuml dependencies
title User Authentication - Module & Technology Dependencies

' Module groupings
package "Authentication System Modules" {
  [Authentication Module] as AUTH
  [Session Management Module] as SESSION
  [User Management Module] as USER
}

' Language/Technology layers
package "Programming Languages" {
  [Java Services\n(5 files)] as JAVA
  [SQL Scripts\n(3 files)] as SQL
  [JavaScript/React\n(4 files)] as JS
}

' External systems
cloud "External Systems" {
  [LDAP Directory] as LDAP
  [Email Service] as EMAIL
}

database "Data Storage" {
  [User Database\nUSERS, SESSIONS, ROLES] as DB
  [Redis Cache] as CACHE
}

' Module-to-language connections
AUTH --> JAVA : AuthenticationManager.java\nPasswordValidator.java
AUTH --> SQL : user_schema.sql\nauth_procedures.sql
AUTH --> JS : LoginForm.jsx\nAuthProvider.jsx

SESSION --> JAVA : SessionManager.java\nTokenGenerator.java
SESSION --> SQL : session_cleanup.sql

USER --> JAVA : UserRepository.java
USER --> SQL : user_crud.sql

' Module-to-module dependencies
AUTH -down-> SESSION : creates sessions\n(createSession)
AUTH -down-> USER : validates credentials\n(getUserByUsername)

' External integrations
AUTH -right-> LDAP : user lookup\n(LDAP bind)
AUTH --> EMAIL : password reset emails
JAVA -down-> DB : INSERT/UPDATE\nUSERS, SESSIONS
SESSION --> CACHE : session storage\n(Redis SET/GET)

note right of AUTH
  **Core Authentication Module**

  Handles user authentication:
  - Login with credentials
  - Password validation
  - Session creation
  - Failed attempt tracking
  - Account lockout
end note

note right of LDAP
  **LDAP Integration**

  Active Directory/LDAP
  corporate user directory
  via LDAP protocol
end note

@enduml
